<title>EGYPT: Egypt sees local maize output at 5 mln tonnes.</title>
<headline>Egypt sees local maize output at 5 mln tonnes.</headline>
<dateline>CAIRO 1997-08-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Egypt's Minister of Supply and Trade Ahmed al-Gueily said on Tuesday that local output of maize would reach five million tonnes this year, state television reported on Tuesday.</p>
<p>It gave no further details, but said bakeries would be producing state-subsidised bread of 80 percent wheat and the rest maize.</p>
<p>- Cairo newsroom +20 2 578 3290/1</p>
</text>
